│                                      ││                                                          │
│                                      ││  LazyGithub is a terminal UI for interacting with        │
│                                      ││  GitHub. You can get started by selecting one of the     │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘│  repositories listed in the table on the left. Once      │
┌─ [2] Pull Requests ──────────────────┐│  you have selected a repository, any issues, pull        │
│ #  Status  Author  Title             ││  requests, and action workflows will be retrieved and    │
│                                      ││  displayed below it.                                     │
│                                      ││                                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘│  Issues, pull requests, and action lists can also be   ▁▁│
┌─ [3] Issues ─────────────────────────┐│  interacted with!                                        │
│ #  Status  Author  Title             ││                                                          │
│                                      ││                                                          │
│                                      ││  Pull Requests                                           │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘│                                                          │
┌─ [4] Workflows ──────────────────────┐│  You can interact with a PR by viewing its details,      │
│ Time  Result  Job Name  Run Name  Run││  viewing the PR diff, and participating in any active    │
│                                   ▎  ││  conversations happening on the PR. You can also         │
│                                      ││  create a new PR for the currently selected repo.        │
│                                      ││                                                          │
